# Moto G20 (java) 2026-09-26: the AOSP vendor.ril-daemon service is DISABLED.
# This definition collided with the SPRD unisoc.rild.rc
# (vendor/etc/init/unisoc.rild.rc) which defines the SAME service name
# "vendor.ril-daemon" pointing at the SPRD urild (/vendor/bin/hw/urild).
# init ignores duplicate service names, and this file parses first
# (alphabetical), so the running "rild" was THIS AOSP binary — which sleeps
# forever in "RIL_Init starting sleep loop" without rild.libpath. The SPRD
# urild never ran. With the SPRD definition active (run as root per the
# unisoc.rild.rc comment), urild registers IRadio/slot1+slot2 and
# IRadioConfig (proven live 2026-09-25).
# service vendor.ril-daemon /vendor/bin/hw/rild
#     class main
#     user radio
#     group radio cache inet misc audio log readproc wakelock
#     capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND NET_ADMIN NET_RAW
